  "notes": "List prices are the struck-through homepage prices. On 2026-10-31 the homepage was running HALLOWEEN codes: BOO (50% off Elite Daily and Ignite, 45% off Instant), BOGO (buy-1-get-1 on Elite Access), MYSTERY (/coupon-code-pricing) and LAUNCHPAD. Elite Daily is a monthly subscription with no activation fee. Elite Access is a $39 one-time eval (the help center states $39; the homepage shows a struck-through $139-$359, which equals the activation fee) plus an activation fee on pass of $139/$189/$259/$359, with 30 days to pass. Instant and Ignite are one-time fees with no evaluation. Elite Daily reset fees differ across pages ($84/$104/$194/$270 on the homepage vs $66/$82/$154/$215 in the help article), probably promo-dependent. The 150K Elite Daily DLL is $1,750 in the homepage eval tab vs $1,850 in the help article/funded tab. Sim payout caps per request: Elite Daily $750-$2,250, Elite Access $1,000-$2,500, Instant 2.0 $1,000-$3,000, Ignite $500-$2,000. Path to live: after 3 payouts (5 on Elite Daily) a risk manager reviews you; then Pre-Live/Live at 80/20 with daily, uncapped payouts. HQ is the Wyoming address in the site footer (Top One Futures, LLC, 1621 Central Ave, Suite 8433, Cheyenne WY 82001), which looks like a registered-agent address. No founding year is published (Trustpilot profile claimed Mar 2025). News: allowed except on Elite Daily/Elite Access funded accounts (no trades 2 min before/after high-impact news). All positions must be closed by 4:10 PM EST, so no overnight or weekend holds. Max allocation is left null because the two homepage figures ($3M vs $1.5M) conflict.",
